T {256-code INL/DNL nominal transfer-curve testbench (DAC-linearity, Gate 3).
ONE long stepped transient covers all 256 codes -- no per-code re-simulation.
Period T=250ns/code: [0,100n) SAMPLE=1 sample phase, DAC_TOP resets toward
a FIXED input VIN=0V (isolates DAC cap linearity from input-dependent
effects per instructions); [100n,250n) SAMPLE=0 convert phase, B0-B7
driven to this code's bits (bit set -> VREF=1.65V, bit clear -> GND),
DAC_TOP settles (>=100ns of margin past the 40ns Gate-2 ceiling) before
the next sample phase. B lines only transition where a bit actually
flips between code k-1 and k, right at each convert-phase boundary, 1ns
edges (matches SAMPLE's edge rate). 20fF comparator-input placeholder
load on DAC_TOP, same as tb_major_carry.sch/tb_sample_hold.sch.
extract_dnl_inl.py (designs/scripts/) reads the wrdata CSV and picks
each code's settled sample 5ns before its convert-phase ends (245n into
each period), computes DNL/INL vs both endpoint and best-fit lines.} 0 -300 0 0 0.25 0.25 {}
